1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,652
Sweetheart, I've hosted family for Christmas for

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:04,945
over fifty years.

3
00:00:05,125 --> 00:00:07,998
Sons, daughters-in-law, grandchildren,

4
00:00:07,998 --> 00:00:10,492
my brother Danny and his snoring,

5
00:00:10,492 --> 00:00:12,836
and one year a cousin from Iowa

6
00:00:12,836 --> 00:00:15,481
I'd never met who stayed nine days.

7
00:00:15,661 --> 00:00:18,547
And I've learned that people don't remember

8
00:00:18,547 --> 00:00:20,224
how fancy your house was.

9
00:00:20,404 --> 00:00:22,605
They remember how you made them feel

10
00:00:22,605 --> 00:00:24,073
when they woke up in it.

11
00:00:24,422 --> 00:00:27,039
So tonight I'm giving you nine things

12
00:00:27,039 --> 00:00:29,373
every Christmas guest room needs,

13
00:00:29,373 --> 00:00:31,423
and they cost almost nothing.

14
00:00:31,603 --> 00:00:34,371
Little things your guests will notice,

15
00:00:34,371 --> 00:00:37,211
and remember, and tell everybody about.

16
00:00:37,391 --> 00:00:38,559
And stay with me,

17
00:00:38,559 --> 00:00:40,827
because the last one is the thing

18
00:00:40,827 --> 00:00:43,369
my Aunt Margaret did for every guest,

19
00:00:43,369 --> 00:00:45,843
and people still talk about it sixty

20
00:00:45,843 --> 00:00:46,667
years later.

21
00:00:47,018 --> 00:00:49,652
My Aunt Margaret lived in Columbus,

22
00:00:49,652 --> 00:00:51,534
in a big old house with a

23
00:00:51,534 --> 00:00:53,642
spare room at the top of the

24
00:00:53,642 --> 00:00:54,169
stairs.

25
00:00:54,349 --> 00:00:56,566
When we visited at Christmas,

26
00:00:56,566 --> 00:00:58,172
I got to sleep there,

27
00:00:58,172 --> 00:00:59,242
all by myself,

28
00:00:59,242 --> 00:01:01,536
in a bed with a white chenille

29
00:01:01,536 --> 00:01:04,288
spread and a hot water bottle tucked

30
00:01:04,288 --> 00:01:05,588
under the covers.

31
00:01:05,768 --> 00:01:07,516
I was nine years old,

32
00:01:07,516 --> 00:01:09,931
and I felt like a princess in

33
00:01:09,931 --> 00:01:10,597
a hotel.

34
00:01:10,948 --> 00:01:12,626
She didn't have money,

35
00:01:12,626 --> 00:01:13,084
honey.

36
00:01:13,264 --> 00:01:16,062
Uncle Walt drove a bread truck.

37
00:01:16,242 --> 00:01:18,737
But she thought about everything a guest

38
00:01:18,737 --> 00:01:20,671
might need in the middle of the

39
00:01:20,671 --> 00:01:22,729
night, and she put it right there

40
00:01:22,729 --> 00:01:24,102
before you had to ask.

41
00:01:24,282 --> 00:01:26,877
That's the whole secret of a good

42
00:01:26,877 --> 00:01:27,741
guest room.

43
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:30,070
In a minute I'll show you the

44
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:32,589
first thing, and it's the one most

45
00:01:32,589 --> 00:01:33,552
hosts forget.

46
00:01:33,903 --> 00:01:36,079
And here's the best way to find

47
00:01:36,079 --> 00:01:38,256
out what your guest room needs.

48
00:01:38,436 --> 00:01:40,027
Sleep in it yourself,

49
00:01:40,027 --> 00:01:42,755
one night, before the company comes.

50
00:01:42,935 --> 00:01:45,294
You'll find out the mattress sags,

51
00:01:45,294 --> 00:01:47,237
the lamp is too far from the

52
00:01:47,237 --> 00:01:49,387
bed, the closet has no hangers,

53
00:01:49,387 --> 00:01:51,538
and the window lets in a draft.

54
00:01:51,718 --> 00:01:54,408
I did this in nineteen seventy-five,

55
00:01:54,408 --> 00:01:56,949
and I fixed eleven things the next

56
00:01:56,949 --> 00:01:57,546
morning.

57
00:01:57,897 --> 00:02:01,043
Number one, the one most hosts forget.

58
00:02:01,223 --> 00:02:03,085
A lamp right by the bed,

59
00:02:03,085 --> 00:02:05,878
that you can turn on without getting

60
00:02:05,878 --> 00:02:06,111
up.

61
00:02:06,291 --> 00:02:08,792
And a little nightlight in the hallway,

62
00:02:08,792 --> 00:02:10,331
and one in the bathroom.

63
00:02:10,511 --> 00:02:12,539
A guest in a strange house at

64
00:02:12,539 --> 00:02:14,007
three in the morning,

65
00:02:14,007 --> 00:02:16,594
looking for the bathroom in the dark,

66
00:02:16,594 --> 00:02:18,832
is how people stub toes and walk

67
00:02:18,832 --> 00:02:19,741
into closets.

68
00:02:19,921 --> 00:02:22,270
My cousin from Iowa walked into my

69
00:02:22,270 --> 00:02:24,618
linen closet and stood there for a

70
00:02:24,618 --> 00:02:25,447
full minute.

71
00:02:25,798 --> 00:02:27,017
Number two.

72
00:02:27,197 --> 00:02:29,984
Extra blankets, folded at the foot of

73
00:02:29,984 --> 00:02:32,168
the bed, or in a basket where

74
00:02:32,168 --> 00:02:33,524
they can see them.

75
00:02:33,704 --> 00:02:35,829
Everybody sleeps different.

76
00:02:36,009 --> 00:02:38,158
Some people are always cold,

77
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:40,690
and they're too polite to ask for

78
00:02:40,690 --> 00:02:41,918
another blanket.

79
00:02:42,098 --> 00:02:44,559
So they lie there shivering all night.

80
00:02:44,739 --> 00:02:47,465
A soft throw and a heavy quilt,

81
00:02:47,465 --> 00:02:50,719
right there, means nobody has to ask.

82
00:02:50,899 --> 00:02:52,615
And an extra pillow,

83
00:02:52,615 --> 00:02:54,846
a soft one and a firm one.

84
00:02:55,196 --> 00:02:56,415
Number three.

85
00:02:56,595 --> 00:02:58,906
A stack of fresh towels on the

86
00:02:58,906 --> 00:03:00,062
bed or a chair,

87
00:03:00,062 --> 00:03:02,760
so they know which ones are theirs.

88
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:04,009
A bath towel,

89
00:03:04,009 --> 00:03:06,642
a hand towel and a washcloth for

90
00:03:06,642 --> 00:03:07,630
each person.

91
00:03:07,810 --> 00:03:10,041
And a little basket with the things

92
00:03:10,041 --> 00:03:10,933
people forget.

93
00:03:11,113 --> 00:03:12,985
A new toothbrush,

94
00:03:12,985 --> 00:03:15,517
small toothpaste, soap,

95
00:03:15,517 --> 00:03:17,389
shampoo, a razor,

96
00:03:17,389 --> 00:03:19,151
a comb, aspirin,

97
00:03:19,151 --> 00:03:21,353
and a phone charger.

98
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:24,161
I keep the little soaps from hotels

99
00:03:24,161 --> 00:03:26,038
all year for this basket.

100
00:03:26,388 --> 00:03:27,985
If this is helping you,

101
00:03:27,985 --> 00:03:30,347
honey, tap the like button for me.

102
00:03:30,527 --> 00:03:33,301
It helps Grandma more than you know.

103
00:03:33,481 --> 00:03:35,652
And put a phone charger by the

104
00:03:35,652 --> 00:03:37,243
bed, with a long cord.

105
00:03:37,423 --> 00:03:40,309
It's the first thing every guest under

106
00:03:40,309 --> 00:03:41,904
sixty asks for today.

107
00:03:42,084 --> 00:03:44,688
My grandson says a guest room without

108
00:03:44,688 --> 00:03:46,800
a charger is like a guest room

109
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:47,785
without a bed.

110
00:03:47,965 --> 00:03:49,653
I think he's exaggerating,

111
00:03:49,653 --> 00:03:50,821
but only a little.

112
00:03:51,171 --> 00:03:52,378
Number four.

113
00:03:52,558 --> 00:03:54,659
Room to put their things.

114
00:03:54,839 --> 00:03:56,651
Clear out half the closet,

115
00:03:56,651 --> 00:03:58,740
and leave a few empty hangers.

116
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:01,300
Empty one drawer in the dresser.

117
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,859
Put a luggage rack,

118
00:04:02,859 --> 00:04:04,818
or just a sturdy chair or a

119
00:04:04,818 --> 00:04:07,793
bench, where they can open their suitcase

120
00:04:07,793 --> 00:04:09,898
without bending to the floor.

121
00:04:10,078 --> 00:04:12,351
Living out of a suitcase on the

122
00:04:12,351 --> 00:04:14,479
floor for a week is the worst

123
00:04:14,479 --> 00:04:16,312
part of visiting anybody.

124
00:04:16,663 --> 00:04:17,632
And a mirror,

125
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:20,318
honey, a full-length one if you can,

126
00:04:20,318 --> 00:04:22,108
on the back of the door.

127
00:04:22,288 --> 00:04:24,512
And a small table or a cleared

128
00:04:24,512 --> 00:04:27,034
spot on the dresser where they can

129
00:04:27,034 --> 00:04:28,591
set out their things,

130
00:04:28,591 --> 00:04:30,593
their glasses, their watch,

131
00:04:30,593 --> 00:04:31,483
their pills.

132
00:04:31,663 --> 00:04:33,892
Older guests especially.

133
00:04:34,072 --> 00:04:36,737
My mother, when she visited me in

134
00:04:36,737 --> 00:04:39,645
her eighties, needed a place for her

135
00:04:39,645 --> 00:04:42,310
pills, her glasses and her Bible,

136
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:43,360
all in a row.

137
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:46,038
So I cleared the dresser top every

138
00:04:46,038 --> 00:04:47,801
Christmas, just for her.

139
00:04:48,151 --> 00:04:49,416
Number five.

140
00:04:49,596 --> 00:04:51,762
A glass and a pitcher or bottle

141
00:04:51,762 --> 00:04:53,648
of water on the nightstand.

142
00:04:53,828 --> 00:04:56,539
And a little plate of Christmas cookies

143
00:04:56,539 --> 00:04:58,555
or a small bowl of candy with

144
00:04:58,555 --> 00:04:59,180
a napkin.

145
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:01,675
People get thirsty and a little hungry

146
00:05:01,675 --> 00:05:02,466
in the night,

147
00:05:02,466 --> 00:05:04,598
and they don't want to go wandering

148
00:05:04,598 --> 00:05:07,034
through your kitchen in their nightgown.

149
00:05:07,214 --> 00:05:09,775
Aunt Margaret left two of her sugar

150
00:05:09,775 --> 00:05:11,165
cookies on a doily,

151
00:05:11,165 --> 00:05:12,555
every single night.

152
00:05:12,905 --> 00:05:14,286
Number six.

153
00:05:14,466 --> 00:05:16,625
A little bit of Christmas in the

154
00:05:16,625 --> 00:05:16,962
room.

155
00:05:17,142 --> 00:05:18,373
Not much.

156
00:05:18,553 --> 00:05:20,579
A small wreath on the door,

157
00:05:20,579 --> 00:05:22,756
a sprig of greenery in a jar,

158
00:05:22,756 --> 00:05:25,083
a tiny lit tree on the dresser,

159
00:05:25,083 --> 00:05:25,983
or a candle.

160
00:05:26,163 --> 00:05:28,370
Just enough so it feels like part

161
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:29,640
of the celebration,

162
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:31,579
not a storage room with a bed

163
00:05:31,579 --> 00:05:31,980
in it.

164
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:34,870
My guest room gets one little ceramic

165
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:37,433
Christmas tree with colored lights,

166
00:05:37,433 --> 00:05:39,045
from nineteen seventy.

167
00:05:39,225 --> 00:05:42,087
The grandchildren fight to sleep next to

168
00:05:42,087 --> 00:05:42,301
it.

169
00:05:42,652 --> 00:05:45,218
So far, a light by the bed,

170
00:05:45,218 --> 00:05:48,640
extra blankets, towels and a basket,

171
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,446
room in the closet,

172
00:05:50,446 --> 00:05:52,157
water and a snack,

173
00:05:52,157 --> 00:05:54,343
and a little Christmas.

174
00:05:54,523 --> 00:05:55,777
Number seven.

175
00:05:55,957 --> 00:05:58,715
A little card with the information they

176
00:05:58,715 --> 00:05:59,068
need.

177
00:05:59,248 --> 00:06:00,955
The Wi-Fi password.

178
00:06:01,135 --> 00:06:03,016
What time breakfast is.

179
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:05,227
Which bathroom is theirs.

180
00:06:05,407 --> 00:06:07,038
Where the coffee is,

181
00:06:07,038 --> 00:06:08,751
if they get up early.

182
00:06:08,931 --> 00:06:11,628
It saves them from asking a dozen

183
00:06:11,628 --> 00:06:13,099
awkward questions.

184
00:06:13,449 --> 00:06:16,663
And tell them about the early riser,

185
00:06:16,663 --> 00:06:17,199
honey.

186
00:06:17,379 --> 00:06:18,514
In my house,

187
00:06:18,514 --> 00:06:19,271
it's me.

188
00:06:19,451 --> 00:06:21,146
I'm up at five-thirty.

189
00:06:21,326 --> 00:06:23,056
So I put a note on the

190
00:06:23,056 --> 00:06:24,236
card that says,

191
00:06:24,236 --> 00:06:25,809
Grandma is up early,

192
00:06:25,809 --> 00:06:27,697
the coffee is on by six,

193
00:06:27,697 --> 00:06:29,191
come down any time,

194
00:06:29,191 --> 00:06:31,787
and don't you dare make your bed.

195
00:06:31,967 --> 00:06:35,670
That last line always makes them smile.

196
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:37,952
And they make the bed anyway.

197
00:06:38,302 --> 00:06:39,393
Number eight.

198
00:06:39,573 --> 00:06:41,477
Quiet and privacy.

199
00:06:41,657 --> 00:06:44,931
A door that closes and stays closed.

200
00:06:45,111 --> 00:06:48,054
Dark curtains, or an extra blanket you

201
00:06:48,054 --> 00:06:49,990
can hang over the window,

202
00:06:49,990 --> 00:06:52,158
so they can sleep past dawn.

203
00:06:52,338 --> 00:06:54,456
And a little fan or a sound

204
00:06:54,456 --> 00:06:56,967
machine to cover the sounds of a

205
00:06:56,967 --> 00:06:57,830
busy house.

206
00:06:58,010 --> 00:07:00,923
Especially if Uncle Danny is snoring down

207
00:07:00,923 --> 00:07:01,562
the hall.

208
00:07:01,742 --> 00:07:04,552
Danny's snoring has been measured.

209
00:07:04,732 --> 00:07:06,717
It's louder than a lawnmower.

210
00:07:07,068 --> 00:07:09,115
And give them time alone,

211
00:07:09,115 --> 00:07:10,017
sweetheart.

212
00:07:10,197 --> 00:07:12,978
When family comes for several days,

213
00:07:12,978 --> 00:07:16,475
everybody needs a little rest from everybody

214
00:07:16,475 --> 00:07:16,872
else.

215
00:07:17,052 --> 00:07:19,003
Don't plan every hour.

216
00:07:19,183 --> 00:07:20,844
Let them sleep late,

217
00:07:20,844 --> 00:07:21,841
take a walk,

218
00:07:21,841 --> 00:07:23,420
read in their room,

219
00:07:23,420 --> 00:07:25,580
or take a nap after lunch.

220
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:28,107
A good host knows when to leave

221
00:07:28,107 --> 00:07:29,394
her guests alone.

222
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:30,972
My mother said,

223
00:07:30,972 --> 00:07:32,929
company is like fish.

224
00:07:33,109 --> 00:07:34,452
After three days,

225
00:07:34,452 --> 00:07:35,953
give them some air.

226
00:07:36,304 --> 00:07:37,876
And now number nine,

227
00:07:37,876 --> 00:07:39,685
Aunt Margaret's secret,

228
00:07:39,685 --> 00:07:42,201
the one people still talk about.

229
00:07:42,381 --> 00:07:44,622
A handwritten note on the pillow.

230
00:07:44,802 --> 00:07:46,637
Just a few lines.

231
00:07:46,817 --> 00:07:49,940
Welcome home, we're so glad you're here.

232
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:51,315
Sleep well.

233
00:07:51,495 --> 00:07:53,771
And one little personal thing.

234
00:07:53,951 --> 00:07:56,719
I remember the first Christmas you came

235
00:07:56,719 --> 00:07:57,074
here.

236
00:07:57,254 --> 00:07:59,991
Or, I made your favorite pie for

237
00:07:59,991 --> 00:08:00,760
tomorrow.

238
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:02,032
That's all.

239
00:08:02,212 --> 00:08:04,267
It takes two minutes to write.

240
00:08:04,617 --> 00:08:05,823
When I was nine,

241
00:08:05,823 --> 00:08:08,764
Aunt Margaret's note on my pillow said,

242
00:08:08,764 --> 00:08:11,329
Ruthie, you are my favorite niece,

243
00:08:11,329 --> 00:08:13,440
but don't tell your cousins.

244
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:16,023
I believed it for thirty years.

245
00:08:16,203 --> 00:08:17,699
Then at her funeral,

246
00:08:17,699 --> 00:08:19,419
in nineteen eighty-six,

247
00:08:19,419 --> 00:08:21,962
all eleven of us cousins found out

248
00:08:21,962 --> 00:08:24,654
she'd written the exact same note to

249
00:08:24,654 --> 00:08:26,374
every single one of us.

250
00:08:26,554 --> 00:08:29,178
We laughed and cried all afternoon.

251
00:08:29,358 --> 00:08:30,716
She was right.

252
00:08:30,896 --> 00:08:32,591
We were all her favorite.

253
00:08:32,941 --> 00:08:34,657
And on the last morning,

254
00:08:34,657 --> 00:08:36,946
a little something for the road.

255
00:08:37,126 --> 00:08:39,083
A small tin of cookies,

256
00:08:39,083 --> 00:08:42,317
a few sandwiches wrapped in wax paper,

257
00:08:42,317 --> 00:08:44,700
or a thermos of coffee for a

258
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:45,636
long drive.

259
00:08:45,816 --> 00:08:48,768
Aunt Margaret always sent us home with

260
00:08:48,768 --> 00:08:51,254
a shoebox of fried chicken and a

261
00:08:51,254 --> 00:08:52,109
pound cake.

262
00:08:52,289 --> 00:08:54,195
We ate it in the car before

263
00:08:54,195 --> 00:08:55,818
we got out of Columbus.

264
00:08:55,998 --> 00:08:58,003
My father said it was the best

265
00:08:58,003 --> 00:08:59,539
part of the whole trip.

266
00:08:59,890 --> 00:09:01,828
And if you don't have a guest

267
00:09:01,828 --> 00:09:04,034
room, honey, you can still do all

268
00:09:04,034 --> 00:09:04,568
of this.

269
00:09:04,748 --> 00:09:06,780
Make up the sofa bed or an

270
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:08,656
air mattress in the den,

271
00:09:08,656 --> 00:09:09,984
with real sheets,

272
00:09:09,984 --> 00:09:12,016
a good pillow and a quilt.

273
00:09:12,196 --> 00:09:14,585
Put a little lamp beside it,

274
00:09:14,585 --> 00:09:16,377
a basket with towels,

275
00:09:16,377 --> 00:09:17,827
water and a note.

276
00:09:18,007 --> 00:09:20,339
Hang a sheet on a tension rod

277
00:09:20,339 --> 00:09:21,304
for privacy.

278
00:09:21,484 --> 00:09:23,788
A well-made sofa bed with a note

279
00:09:23,788 --> 00:09:26,235
is better than a fancy room nobody

280
00:09:26,235 --> 00:09:27,243
thought about.

281
00:09:27,593 --> 00:09:29,857
And make it easy on yourself,

282
00:09:29,857 --> 00:09:30,716
sweetheart.

283
00:09:30,896 --> 00:09:33,404
Wash the sheets and towels the week

284
00:09:33,404 --> 00:09:35,841
before, and get the room ready two

285
00:09:35,841 --> 00:09:38,493
days early, so you're not making beds

286
00:09:38,493 --> 00:09:41,144
at midnight on Christmas Eve when the

287
00:09:41,144 --> 00:09:42,076
car pulls in.

288
00:09:42,256 --> 00:09:44,411
Then shut the door and don't touch

289
00:09:44,411 --> 00:09:44,601
it.

290
00:09:44,781 --> 00:09:47,082
Your guests will walk in and think

291
00:09:47,082 --> 00:09:48,705
you did it all by magic.

292
00:09:49,056 --> 00:09:50,391
So one more time.

293
00:09:50,571 --> 00:09:52,672
Sleep in it yourself first.

294
00:09:52,852 --> 00:09:55,347
A lamp by the bed and nightlights

295
00:09:55,347 --> 00:09:56,254
in the hall.

296
00:09:56,434 --> 00:09:58,942
Extra blankets and pillows.

297
00:09:59,122 --> 00:10:02,428
Towels, and a basket of forgotten things,

298
00:10:02,428 --> 00:10:03,638
with a charger.

299
00:10:03,818 --> 00:10:05,141
Room in the closet.

300
00:10:05,321 --> 00:10:07,423
Water and two cookies.

301
00:10:07,603 --> 00:10:09,124
A little Christmas.

302
00:10:09,304 --> 00:10:11,642
A card with the Wi-Fi and the

303
00:10:11,642 --> 00:10:12,206
coffee.

304
00:10:12,386 --> 00:10:14,580
Quiet and dark curtains.

305
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:17,326
And a handwritten note on the pillow.

306
00:10:17,506 --> 00:10:19,937
That's how Aunt Margaret made every one

307
00:10:19,937 --> 00:10:21,744
of us feel like her favorite.

308
00:10:22,094 --> 00:10:23,845
Tell me in the comments,

309
00:10:23,845 --> 00:10:24,648
sweetheart.

310
00:10:24,828 --> 00:10:27,549
Who's coming to your house for Christmas

311
00:10:27,549 --> 00:10:28,229
this year?

312
00:10:28,409 --> 00:10:30,569
Or are you the one traveling?

313
00:10:30,749 --> 00:10:33,929
The whole playlist of Grandma's Christmas tips

314
00:10:33,929 --> 00:10:36,003
is right there on your screen,

315
00:10:36,003 --> 00:10:37,939
and I'll see you in the next

316
00:10:37,939 --> 00:10:38,353
video.

317
00:10:38,533 --> 00:10:40,089
Good night, honey.

318
00:10:40,269 --> 00:10:41,720
Merry Christmas.
